 The session cookie is also applied to error responses, so a request that throws still slides the window and still persists a session created during it.
 
+## Rotate the Password
+
+To change `password` without signing everyone out, keep the previous password in `extraUnsealPasswords`. H3 seals every cookie with `password` and tries the extra passwords only when opening one:
+
+```js
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: "new-80d42cfb-1cd2-462c-8f17-e3237d9027e9", // seals new cookies
+  extraUnsealPasswords: ["80d42cfb-1cd2-462c-8f17-e3237d9027e9"], // opens older cookies only
+  maxAge: 60 * 60 * 24 * 7,
+});
+```
+
+A session opened with an extra password is moved to `password` the next time it is written or slid under `idleTimeout`, so the migration happens gradually and no session is reset in bulk. To rotate safely:
+
+1. Set the new password in `password` and move the old one to `extraUnsealPasswords`.
+2. Wait until every session sealed with the old password has passed `maxAge` or `idleTimeout`, or has been written. Until then, keep the old password in the list.
+3. Remove the old password from `extraUnsealPasswords`. Any session still sealed with it is signed out.
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> Rotation needs `maxAge` or `idleTimeout`. Without either, a session that is never written never expires, so it keeps the old password valid and you cannot remove it without signing that session out.
+
+> [!WARNING]
+> An old password in `extraUnsealPasswords` keeps working until you remove it, including when it has been compromised. Removing it is your responsibility.
+
+Each extra password adds one PBKDF2 derivation to every request that carries a cookie no password opens. Keep the list short.
+
 ## Use Multiple Sessions
 
 Because each session is stored under its own `name`, you can run several independent sessions on the same request. They live in separate cookies and never overwrite each other, which is useful for keeping unrelated concerns apart, such as a long-lived auth session and a short-lived flash message:
